      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Add regtest – and do something good with",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "RWSycnrhonzied<> x;",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "Auto cl = x.cget ();",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "Auto rwl = x.rwget ();\t// ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "// See ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/24334735/can-a-shared-lock-on-a-stdshared-timed-mutex-be-upgraded-to-an-exclusive-lock"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/24334735/can-a-shared-lock-on-a-stdshared-timed-mutex-be-upgraded-to-an-exclusive-lock",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "// ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "http://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/papers/2012/n3427.html"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "http://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/papers/2012/n3427.html",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "DECIDE what I want to do (probably to make it easy/automatic) – and implement that. AND DOCUMENT. Now not documented, but on gcc – just hangs. ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "MAYBE overload of rwget() taking previous read lock to upgrade? That CTOR of WriteableLock taking ref to prev readable, which it unlocks, and then relocks in DTOR. That seems safe and portable. And document (assert) no OTHER shared_locks from THIS THREAD possible. So you CAN upgrade lock – just have to be explicit about it.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "OR – maybe use:",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "https://github.com/HowardHinnant/upgrade_mutex"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "https://github.com/HowardHinnant/upgrade_mutex",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
